=== The deletion day  (2026-01-22) ===
Accounts are deleted, but only where the gate opens: a confirmed hand-over, no laptop
still bound to the person, and no identity a live colleague claims.


--- notification (leaver.blocked) would be sent to IT ---
subject: Deletion blocked (devices_bound): Robin Ellis

Deletion blocked: Robin Ellis (robin.ellis@example.com)

Reason: devices_bound

- Demo field laptop, windows, serial DEMOSERIAL1

Nothing has been deleted. The row stays in offboarding and the deletion is
attempted again on the next run once the reason clears.

This note is sent when the blocking set CHANGES, and re-raised once a week.
Silence therefore means the same blockage, not a resolved one. See docs/runbooks/clear-a-blocked-deletion.md.

--- end notification ---

--- notification (leaver.day7) would be sent to IT ---
subject: Day 7 complete: Sam Rivera

Day 7 offboarding complete: Sam Rivera (sam.rivera@example.com)

- Identity provider account: identity provider account deleted, confirmed gone
- Google account: Google account deleted, confirmed gone
- Devices bound at the moment of deletion: none
- Files were handed to: jane.doe@example.com

This person is now recorded as departed. That row is a tombstone and is never
removed: it is what stops a later HR sync seeing an old leaver as a new one and
starting the whole sequence again.

--- end notification ---

